      "solution": "num = \"123456789\"\na = input()\nf = 0\nl = 0\nb = True\nfor i in range(len(a)):\n    if a[i] in num:\n        l = i\n        if b:\n            b = False\n            f = i\nsig_figs = (l+1)-f\nperiod = a.find(\".\")\nif period!=-1:\n    for i in range(l+1,len(a)):\n        if a[i]==\"0\":\n            sig_figs+=1\nprint(sig_figs)\n",
      "statement": "Given an string, [[n]], determine [[sig figs]], the number of significant figures present.\n\n[[sig figs]] can be determined by four rules:\n1. The numbers {{1-9}} are always significant.\n2. Any {{zeros}} before the first occurrence of {{1-9}} is <<never>> significant.\n3. Any {{zeros}} between occurrences of {{1-9}} are <<always>> significant.\n4. {{Zeros}} after the last occurrence of {{1-9}} are only significant if there is a decimal present <<anywhere>> in the number.",
