    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Given an string, <var>n</var>, determine <var>sig figs</var>, the number of significant figures present.<br><br><var>sig figs</var> can be determined by four rules:<br>1. The numbers <const>1-9</const> are always significant.<br>2. Any <const>zeros</const> before the first occurrence of <const>1-9</const> is <strong>never</strong> significant.<br>3. Any <const>zeros</const> between occurrences of <const>1-9</const> are <strong>always</strong> significant.<br>4. <const>Zeros</const> after the last occurrence of <const>1-9</const> are only significant if there is a decimal present <strong>anywhere</strong> in the number.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> a string, <var>n</var></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><var>sig_figs</var>, the number of significant figures determined by the rules above.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\"></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">0.0000005090</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">4</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
